Thanks Chris.  I'll just add that you need specify exactly where the
tiles file is to the PocketPc since there is no concept of a "current
directory" in the way that WindowsCE handles files.  Most cards in
PocketPC's are named 'Storage Card' but sometimes there's an internal
flash memory so the removable card becomes 'Storage Card2' or
something like that.

So taking your example in my case the first line becomes:

  OPTIONS=3Dtile_file:\Storage Card\Program Files\Net Hack
\tiles20x10c.bmp,tile_height:20,tile_width:10

It's worth noting that when you install Nethack for PocketPC via a cab
file and you specify the Storage Card for the installation it will put
it in /Storage Card/Program Files/Nethack 3.43 for (blah blah some
long directory name).  I change the directory name to just "Net Hack"
to save headaches later on.

